/P 1308 0 R
/E ("You can't get pregnant during menstruation." Although the likelihood is lower, pregnancy is still possible because ovulation can overlap with menstruation.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
665 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1309 0 R
/E ("Menstrual pain is something you simply have to endure." This is false. Mild discomfort and pain are common, but severe, debilitating pain should be reported to your doctor.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
666 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1310 0 R
/E ("A normal cycle must always start on the same date." The menstrual cycle does not always last the same amount of time, and the start date of menstruation may vary each month. However, significant changes and irregular cycles should be reported to a doctor.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
667 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1311 0 R
/E ("PMS is 'made up' or exaggerated." This is false. PMS has a clear hormonal basis and affects most people who menstruate to varying degrees.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
668 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 181 0 R
/Pg 37 0 R
/A [1312 0 R 0]
/K [9]
>>
